			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young woman whose appearance is derived from <Picture 1>, with a slender oval face, warm light complexion, natural bare-faced skin texture, dark almond-shaped eyes, straight black hair tied into a low ponytail, a plain white crew-neck T-shirt, and a calm neutral expression.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target is a 10.00-second cinematic character video that uses <Picture 1> only as the visual identity reference for <Subject 1>, without using it as a first frame, last frame, keyframe, or composition anchor. The video opens with a distant wide shot of <Subject 1> standing beside a large window in a minimalist room, followed by a gradual camera approach as she turns toward the daylight.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the woman’s facial identity, facial proportions, warm light complexion, natural bare-faced appearance, dark almond-shaped eyes, straight black low ponytail, plain white crew-neck T-shirt, and restrained expression from <Picture 1> remain consistent throughout the video.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses cinematic live-action realism, natural skin texture, restrained colors, soft morning daylight, and smooth stabilized camera movement. <Picture 1> supplies only the identity and appearance of <Subject 1>; it does not determine the opening frame, ending frame, pose, camera angle, or composition.\n\n[Shot 1] A distant wide shot opens directly inside a quiet minimalist apartment. A large floor-to-ceiling window fills the right side of the background, while pale beige walls, a light wooden floor, sheer curtains, and a single low wooden bench define the uncluttered room. <Subject 1> stands near the window in the right third of the frame, shown from head to toe and occupying only a small portion of the composition. She retains the slender oval face, warm light complexion, natural bare-faced skin, dark almond-shaped eyes, straight black hair tied into a low ponytail, and plain white crew-neck T-shirt derived from <Picture 1>. Her outfit is completed with loose light-beige trousers and simple white shoes. Her body faces the window while her head rests at a subtle three-quarter angle. Soft daylight outlines her profile and ponytail without changing her facial identity.\n\nDuring the opening seconds, the camera holds the static distant wide shot as <Subject 1> breathes naturally and shifts her weight slightly from one foot to the other. A gentle breeze moves the sheer curtains, a few loose strands near her forehead, and the lower edge of her T-shirt. She slowly raises her chin and looks through the window.\n\nAt 00:03.500, the camera begins to push in with small amplitude at slow speed, preserving the surrounding architecture and maintaining a full-body composition. <Subject 1> gradually turns her head away from the window and looks toward the camera with the same calm, restrained expression derived from <Picture 1>. Her movement remains slow and anatomically natural, with no abrupt pose changes.\n\nAt 00:07.500, the camera settles into a medium-long shot that still shows her from approximately the knees upward. She blinks once, relaxes her shoulders, and lets her gaze drift slightly past the lens. The camera holds this stable composition until the video ends at 00:10.000. Her face, hairstyle, skin texture, body proportions, and clothing remain stable throughout, with no identity drift, facial morphing, exaggerated expression, additional people, or sudden environmental changes.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nQuiet indoor room tone continues throughout the video, accompanied by faint distant city ambience outside the window. The breeze produces soft curtain movement and subtle fabric rustling.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nSparse solo-piano notes play at a slow tempo with long intervals between notes, remaining low in volume and fading out at 00:10.000.",
